course: dictionary
lesson: 3186
title: Words That Lift You Up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Encouragement is words or actions that give someone confidence and hope to keep going. «Her coach gave her words of encouragement before the race.» The coach's words made the runner feel brave enough to keep trying, so encouragement is help that gives you courage.
explain: The word comes from encourage, which contains courage. Encouragement is a noun that you can give, shout, or receive. «With a little encouragement, Sam finally tried the high dive.» Sam needed a small push of support before he could try something new.
explain: Encouragement can also mean making something more likely to happen. Check which meaning fits by swapping in a simple word, such as help or support, and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Encouragement is a noun, and it is usually uncountable: you say some encouragement, not an encouragement.
fact: Encouragement means words or actions that give someone confidence and hope to keep going.
fact: Encouragement can also mean making something more likely to happen.
fact: Useful phrases: «words of encouragement», «give encouragement», «with a little encouragement», «shout encouragement».
fact: «Honest, gentle encouragement helps people improve.» Kind, truthful support helps someone get better at something.
exercise: «Her coach gave her words of encouragement before the race.» What is encouragement in this sentence? | Tiredness after running | A loud noise from the crowd | *Words that give confidence to keep going | A prize for winning
exercise: «With a little encouragement, Sam finally tried the high dive.» Find and copy the word that names the support Sam received. | *encouragement | finally | high | dive
exercise: «Honest, gentle encouragement helps people improve.» What does encouragement help people do? | Stop trying | *Improve | Forget what they learned | Hide from others
test: «The crowd began to shout encouragement as the runner rounded the last bend.» What does shout encouragement mean here? | Shout at someone to make them stop | *Call out words to cheer someone on | Quietly leave the track | Hand out tickets to the race
test: Which sentence uses encouragement to mean making something more likely to happen? | Her encouragement was a kind word and a smile | *Warm sunshine gave encouragement to the seeds to sprout | Sam gave encouragement to his friend after the match | Coach gave the team words of encouragement
exam: Which word best describes kind words from a friend that help you keep going? | *encouragement | distance | silence | discouragement
